{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe coordinator and fuse remain inert until non-create families route through them. Cutover must preserve independent work, explicitly defer matching plans, and prove the new fuse would not have prematurely stopped historical successful or partially successful jobs.\n\n## Outcome\nMake typed coordination authoritative for non-create families behind an internal per-family rollback selector, persist explicit deferral metadata, add the new endpoint-failure scoped fuse (retaining the blast-radius mass-mutation guard `classify.check_blast_radius`), and emit exact pass outcomes.\n\n## Plan\n1. Venue-gate verified-fake Cloud/DC summary behavior, then change the internal operation-family default from legacy to coordinator; never dual-send.\n2. Route update, delete, probe, clean-label, repair-property, and conflict plans through coordinator/fuse. Preserve successful effects and recover rollback by re-observation.\n3. Defer remaining matching plans with scope/reason/`retry_not_before`; let independent scopes continue.\n4. Preserve exact applied/failed/deferred/skipped/recovered tallies and nonzero degraded-pass signaling.\n5. Replay the sanitized 1,200-run completed GitHub Actions slice. Count only normalized terminal outcomes, never warning/grep text, and prove zero premature termination of observed successful/partial work.\n\n## Testing\nVerified-fake batches assert wire order/call ceilings/tallies/logs/exit. Historical replay names any counterfactual stop and blocks if it predates observed later success.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each non-create family has one coordinator route and one internal legacy rollback value with no dual-send.\n- [ ] Venue-gated Cloud/DC verified fakes pass before the coordinator default changes.\n- [ ] Matching remaining work is deferred with exact scope, reason, and `retry_not_before`, while independent scopes continue.\n- [ ] Applied, failed, deferred, skipped, and recovered tallies plus degraded exit status are exact.\n- [ ] Migrated families route failure fusing through the new endpoint-failure scoped fuse; legacy ad-hoc retry nesting is unreachable for them and the blast-radius mass-mutation guard remains in force.\n- [ ] Historical replay of the completed 1,200-run slice shows zero premature stop before observed successful or partially successful work.\n\n## Out of scope\nCreate coordination remains S4; final legacy removal remains S5."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787555556791897001,"uuid":"a92d0688-0b31-47b8-9b8a-26f6eedbfa02"}